# sandcastle-kit credentials. `sandcastle setup` writes this file for you; to
# do it by hand, copy it to ~/.config/sandcastle-kit/.env (NOT into this repo),
# chmod 600, and uncomment the lines you use. A project can override any key in
# its own <project>/.sandcastle/.env. Empty values are refused, so leave unused
# lines commented out.

# Claude Code subscription token - run `claude setup-token` on your machine.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ...or an Anthropic API key instead (billed per token). Use one of the two.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# GitHub FINE-GRAINED token (github_pat_...), used by the agents inside the
# sandbox to read and comment on issues. Classic (ghp_) and OAuth (gho_)
# tokens are refused: they could push or edit workflows.
# Create: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# Repository access: only the repos you run Sandcastle on.
# Permissions: Issues - Read and write; Metadata - Read.
# GH_TOKEN=

# Optional: a Linear personal API key (read-only is enough), only for projects
# that set `blockers.linear` in .sandcastle/config.ts. Read on the host to see
# whether a `Blocked by ENG-42` issue is done; never passed to a sandbox.
# Keep it in THIS file only: a project's .sandcastle/.env is forwarded into
# every container, so the kit refuses the key there.
# LINEAR_API_KEY=
